This repository holds code under more than one licence.

From ReaKit FX 1.6.0, GainKit Plus 1.0.30 and EON Floatter 1.0.10 (2026-11-04), EON
Studios' own effects and scripts are under the EON Free Licence 1.0 (LICENSE-EON-FREE.md
beside this file): free to use in any work, not for sale or redistribution. That covers
GainKit, Stereo Width, Filter, Quezy (its plugin file, qz_face and qz_engine), the GainKit
Plus and ReaKit FX scripts, EON Floatter, the templates and the track icons. Versions
released before that date keep the MIT licence they were released under.

The MIT licence below covers the ReaKit/ includes (the ReaKit library: knobs, buttons,
sliders, meters, rk_* and the other shared files), apart from qz_face and qz_engine.
Parts ported from other authors' MIT code (Quezy's engine after Justin Johnson's ReEQ,
rk_svf, rk_spectrum, rk_svf_match after Yuriy Ivantsov) keep those authors' MIT notices,
in the files themselves.

It does NOT cover the four effects built on other authors' DSP. Saturation, 3-Band EQ
and DDC keep Michael Gruhn's (LOSER) terms; the De-Esser keeps Lubomir I. Ivanov's
(Liteon) GPL, whose full text is beside it (Eon_JSFX/FX/DeEsser_ReaKit.GPL-3.0.md).
Each of those plugin files carries its author's original header, and LICENSE.md gives
the details.

